  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 123 PM MST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nHigh pressure settling over the Texas Panhandle will bring light\nbut steady east winds to the area overnight, keeping a relatively\ncooler air mass in place. Meanwhile, confidence is increasing for\nrain chances Friday Night into Saturday as models have trended\ntowards a closed-low/further south scenario that will allow more\nmoisture to get pulled into the area. Total rainfall amounts are \nstill expected to be light to moderate, and highest near and east\nof the Rio Grande.\n\nExpect rain showers to slowly develop in SW New Mexico Friday\nafternoon, spreading east along the international border in the\nevening and overnight. Rain will linger the longest east of El\nPaso on Saturday. Cooler temperatures will accompany the showers\nand widespread cloud cover. Highs on Saturday look to stay stuck\nin the upper-50s over much of the lowlands, or about 10-15 degrees\nbelow normal.\n\nTemperatures will warm back up to near normal by Wednesday.",
